### Why use variables?

Variables solve a problem every documentation system faces: **content drift**.

Imagine your product name appears in twenty different step files. You rebrand. Now you must find and update every single occurrence — and miss one, and your documentation looks unprofessional.

Or imagine a screenshot that appears in five guides. The UI changes. You must replace five copies of the image, hoping you caught them all.

Variables fix this by keeping the **source in one place**.


### The benefits

| Benefit | What it means in practice |
|---------|---------------------------|
| **Single source of truth** | Update the variable once, every reference updates automatically |
| **No drift** | Multiple copies of the same text cannot diverge over time |
| **Path tracking** | When you define a URL or image path as a variable, Docs Assembler tracks it. Move, copy, or clone the file, and the path is automatically corrected for the new location |
| **Consistency** | The same warning, the same product name, the same screenshot every time |
| **Easier maintenance** | Less text to review, less to translate, less to keep in sync |

